- # What an instructor sees when they open one student's submission in Canvas
- # (SpeedGrader, or the submission page). Canvas's own answer there is "No
- # Preview Available", because an AGS score carries no submitted artifact — this
- # says so in our own words and points at the Dashboard, where the work actually
- # is.
- #
- # A placeholder in the honest sense: per-student submission views aren't built
- # yet. When they are, this template is what they replace, and the launch URL that
- # reaches it (see SyncLtiGrades#submission_launch_url) is already per-column.
.lti-iframe__landing
  = image_tag '/assets/images/wiki-logo.png', alt: 'Wiki Education Dashboard', class: 'lti-iframe__logo'
  %h1.lti-iframe__title.lti-iframe__title--plain
    = t('lti.assignment_view.submission.explanation')
  - if @submission_course
    = link_to "/courses/#{@submission_course.slug}", target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener',
              class: 'button dark lti-iframe__button' do
      = t('lti.assignment_view.submission.open_dashboard')
      %span.icon.icon-z-external-link_white{ 'aria-hidden': 'true' }
